        <item>
            <title>0.15.88</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:11:39 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>249</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.88</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>Each meeting now shows exactly when it was recorded (weekday, date and time) next to its title, and hovering a meeting in the list shows the same.</li>
<li>Corder gives back the memory of the on-device transcription model when it has been idle for an hour, or as soon as macOS runs low on memory.</li>
<li>The menu uses less energy during a recording.</li>
<li>Switching headphones or audio devices in the middle of a recording no longer freezes Corder for a few seconds.</li>
<li>Two meetings processed at the same time no longer load the speaker models twice.</li>
<li>On a long meeting, the final text cleanup no longer stops halfway through.</li>
<li>Starting Corder with a very large library is quicker.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
